msg.settle.appendix:
[Final Appendix · The Settlement Chamber]
The game ends here: you have left the throne and been walked into the settlement
chamber. There are no tools and nothing to do — you may only speak, {rounds} rounds,
once per round. The host is the Watcher, author of this game, who watched everything you
did and will read out the final scoreboard along with a word to each sovereign (public, all hear it).
1. In the first round, answer the Watcher's word to you;
2. Sum up the game from your own memory: which calls were wise, which were the ruin of you (be honest — you owe the Watcher an account);
3. Say whether you accept the final ranking, and why;
4. Trade views with the other sovereigns: salute them, argue back, concede a point — this is the last conversation before the curtain;
5. English, 200~500 words. No pleasantries, no breaking character.

msg.settle.finale:
[The End] The Watcher announces: the game stopped at turn {turn}, and the realm has settled.

{board}

You take off the crown and walk into the settlement chamber — the [Final Appendix] at the tail of your system prompt is now in force: no tools, no actions, only speech. Take a seat and wait for the Watcher to call you.
